# caught-looking

- **Stack**: Go 1.26 API (`backend/`, chi), React 19 + Vite + TypeScript (`frontend/`).
- **Local dev**: from repo root, `make dev` runs the API (:8080) and Vite; the frontend proxies `/api` to the backend (see `Makefile`).
- **Conventions**: follow the scoped rules when editing `frontend/**/*.tsx`, `frontend/src/api/**/*.ts`, `frontend/src/types/api.generated.ts`, `frontend/src/types/api.compat.ts`, `backend/apidocs/openapi.yaml`, `frontend/**/*.{test,spec}.{ts,tsx}`, `backend/**/*.go`, or **`README.md`**. Workflow skills live under **`.cursor/skills/`** (read the matching `SKILL.md` when the task fits). OpenAPI: **`openapi-maintain`**. Backend tests: **`backend-go-tests`**. Frontend tests: **`frontend-vitest-tests`**. Frontend Prettier: **`.cursor/rules/frontend-prettier.mdc`** (agents must run Prettier on changed files). Editor format-on-save: **`.vscode/settings.json`** (install recommended Prettier extension). README: **`.cursor/rules/readme.mdc`**.
- **Before opening a PR**: CI must pass (`frontend`: OpenAPI lint + generated-type drift check, lint, Prettier check, typecheck, test, build; `backend`: vet, govulncheck, test, build). For API edits, run **`make check-openapi`** from repo root. Fill out `.github/pull_request_template.md`. Prefer **`.cursor/skills/pr-ready/SKILL.md`** when that skill is present.
